lesson k-clapping-names v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=8 subject=music levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Clapping names"
  goal "Clap the beats in a word, count the claps, and say which of two words has more."

  look {
    scene 24x9 {
      minibeasts bugs kinds=["bee", "spider", "butterfly"] spots=4 legs=false at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
      Say bee and clap: one clap. Say spi-der: two claps. Say but-ter-fly: three claps. Every part
      of a word you say is one clap, however many letters it has.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.claps-in-word w="rocket" level=medium
    }
    practice k.claps-in-word count=2 seed=2
    practice k.claps-minibeast count=3 seed=3 easy-count=2
    practice k.more-claps count=2 seed=4 easy-count=1
    show k.clap-ladybird
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.odd-claps k=0 hard-k=2
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.three-claps n=2 easy-n=1 hard-n=3
  }
  remember {
    say "One clap for each part of the word you say."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Say each word naturally and clap together; the child does not need to read the words. A hand
    under the chin helps, since the chin drops once for each part. Long words with few claps, like
    kite, are worth a second go. The clapped question is judged on the music page; on paper, you
    are the judge. Off the page, clap everyone's name at teatime, and the names of the toys. Japan,
    幼稚園教育要領 (kindergarten guidelines), 表現, 内容 (1): "生活の中で様々な音，色，形，手触り，動きなどに気付いたり，感じたりするなどして楽しむ。"
    (Notice and enjoy the sounds, colours, shapes, textures and movements around them.)
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level the words have one or two claps, one is clapped in the teacher's pen first, and the minibeasts are the bee, the snail and the spider."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the words have two or three claps, the minibeasts include the ladybird and the butterfly, and the three-star asks for three claps."
  }
}
